task: raft-compaction
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/raft-compaction
worktree: ../okay-wt-snap

why: stage 2b, the open half of persist-raft stage 2: a
  Raft-replicated data log cannot run unbounded without compaction,
  and a follower that missed a compacted stretch needs the paper's
  InstallSnapshot (§7). The simulator now makes it testable the
  honest way — the minority cut off while the majority commits and
  compacts, then healed and restored from a snapshot, safety
  asserted after every event.

what: RaftState gains snapshotIndex/Term/Members/Data; every log
  access goes through index arithmetic against the snapshot;
  Raft.compact(upTo, snapshot) drops the log up to an applied index
  the ENGINE has snapshotted (the bytes are the engine's, the core
  never reads them); replication sends InstallSnapshot when a
  follower's nextIndex is inside the snapshot; a follower installs
  it (keeps a suffix its last entry agrees with, else discards), and
  `restored` tells the engine to reset its state machine. Wire:
  Node.compact and onRestore. RaftStore does not compact yet (its
  local Store's snapshot is stage 2c). Sim: per-node state machines,
  periodic compaction, the partition scenario now forces snapshots.
